WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.679 --> 00:00:05.640
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie, All Hail Queen
Kuvira.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.431
Since Book 4 starts tomorrow and we already
know who one of the big antagonists is going

00:00:07.431 --> 00:00:12.379
to be I wanted to do my TOP 10 Villains.

00:00:12.379 --> 00:00:18.690
Based on Translations, this says “All Hail
Queen Kuvira”.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:32.059
You could also say “President Kuvira’.

00:00:32.059 --> 00:00:37.150
Quick reminder, the weekly Korra Giveaway
is back, all you have to do to participate

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:40.650
is be a subscriber and leave a comment on
this video.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.620
Here we go, starting with number 10 - Right
of the bat Kuvira

00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:48.060
She goes at the bottom of the list because
it’s the beginning of the season and she’s

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:49.680
an unproven villain.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.719
I have very high expectations for her.

00:00:51.719 --> 00:00:56.800
She is going to be one of if not THE last
villain on an avatar tv series.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:00:59.800
So she’s got these other 9 people she’s
got to out evil.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:05.810
When I saw the book 4 trailer she reminded
me a lot of Ozai when he crowned himself the

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:08.350
phoenix king in front of all those legions.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:18.840
I’m going into the new season with an open
mind, so we’ll see what she’s got.

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:21.070
Number 9 - Koh the Face Stealer

00:01:21.070 --> 00:01:25.300
Still haven’t gotten a good answer where
he or she is in present day.

00:01:25.300 --> 00:01:28.180
Probably waiting for another Avatar to come
along.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:33.350
This was really intended to be a villain to
make Aang doubt himself, which is why it was

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.979
a spirit world character.

00:01:34.979 --> 00:01:37.229
It was all about messing with his head.

00:01:37.229 --> 00:01:40.250
You could argue that all of Korra’s villains
have done that to her in some way.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:41.250
Just made her question her identity.

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.810
Especially Zaheer in book 3.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:46.860
I think that’s the real reason we haven’t
seen Koh in the Korra series, just because

00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:50.659
they gave the role he serves in the story
to physical world villains.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:53.330
I won’t be upset if we don’t see him.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.079
I mean we did get to see Wan Shi Tong.

00:01:57.079 --> 00:01:59.280
Number 8 - Unalaq and Unavaatu

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:04.200
I’m including Unalaq and the Dark Avatar
in this same one.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.200
I wasn’t really happy with the way the character
turned out, but I do have to give props for

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.799
the big twist on the avatar lineage.

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:15.569
This all depended on the introduction of Vaatu
to the story, who I also included on this

00:02:15.569 --> 00:02:20.290
list separately, but I feel like we didn’t
spend enough time with Unalaq before things

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.290
went crazy.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:22.290
Because episodes are so short and each narrative
arc is only 13 or so episodes.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:23.290
You really don’t have time to give the villain
a lot of their own episodes.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:25.419
A lot of the best Last Airbender Villains
were the best because we got to see them evolve

00:02:25.419 --> 00:02:26.419
across the entire series.

00:02:26.419 --> 00:02:27.510
They weren’t limited to a single arc.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:33.769
I also felt like the final boss form of Unavaatu
didn’t turn out to be the terrifying villain

00:02:33.769 --> 00:02:35.939
you want to end the season on.

00:02:35.939 --> 00:02:40.409
There were a whole lot of other pacing and
story issues I had with the Book 2 finale,

00:02:40.409 --> 00:02:45.489
but Unalaq and the dark avatar felt like great
villains that just didn’t pan out the way

00:02:45.489 --> 00:02:47.700
they were originally imagined.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:53.930
I feel like they had a great idea when they
thought of him.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.249
Number 7 - Zuko from Book 1 of Last Airbender

00:02:58.249 --> 00:03:01.849
A lot of the best characters start out at
one end of the spectrum and swing to the other

00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:03.340
by the end of a series.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:07.999
Zuko had the benefit of being a main character
that wasn’t always defined by his relationship

00:03:07.999 --> 00:03:09.569
with the avatar.

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.540
He started out that way, but then we got to
see him in this big family arc in the fire

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:17.480
nation and his sojourn to the earth kingdom.

00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:21.629
There haven’t been a lot of Avatar Characters
that got so much time dedicated to them.

00:03:21.629 --> 00:03:29.620
Which is probably why the others aren’t
so memorable.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:33.629
The reason he’s not higher on the list is
because while he is one of the best Avatar

00:03:33.629 --> 00:03:37.669
characters in general, he was pretty lousy
as a villain.

00:03:37.669 --> 00:03:44.290
Aang just kept running circles around him.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.209
Number 6 - Firelord Sozin

00:03:46.209 --> 00:03:48.849
Here’s someone who knew how to get an evil
job done.

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:51.450
There’s a reason it’s called Sozin’s
Comet.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:57.069
I really miss flashbacks in the Korra series,
there were so many good last airbender flashback

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.069
stories.

00:03:58.069 --> 00:04:01.790
Sozin’s is one of the most important because
it tells the tale of how the 100 year war

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:02.790
began.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.949
He’d go down in history as one of the most
successful warlords ever.

00:04:06.949 --> 00:04:13.529
It was a 100 year war though, so he only presided
over the escalation.

00:04:13.529 --> 00:04:19.459
The clean up job mostly fell on his son Azulon
and then his grandson Ozai really dropped

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:20.459
the ball.

00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:24.999
The twist on Korra now is that it’s the
Metal Bending Tribe that’s bullying everyone.

00:04:24.999 --> 00:04:26.729
Number 5 - Vaatu

00:04:26.729 --> 00:04:33.060
I really liked the concept for this character
but I feel like he and raava were brought

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.710
out too soon.

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:39.210
I understand that right after doing a human
villain, Amon, Bryke didn’t want to do the

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:41.860
exact same thing so they rolled out a spiritual
villain.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:46.889
But when you start talking about universal
concepts like good and evil it feels too big

00:04:46.889 --> 00:04:49.780
to be sandwiched in the middle of a series.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:53.020
Korra defeated Vaatu, so it’s like saying
Korra defeated Evil.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.370
Vaatu is the essence of evil.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:59.320
So it’s kind of ridiculous when you vanquish
the sum of all evil in the universe and you

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:01.250
still have two more giant story arcs.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:06.669
That’s why I feel like they should have
pushed re-opening the spirit portals and “balancing”

00:05:06.669 --> 00:05:08.889
raava and vaatu to the end of book 4.

00:05:08.889 --> 00:05:12.259
It’s okay if you don’t agree, but I feel
like ending on something like that would be

00:05:12.259 --> 00:05:18.759
the best way to tee up the expanded material
and the comics to tell the story of how the

00:05:18.759 --> 00:05:23.910
world learned to live with the spirits like
they did before Avatar Wan.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:27.050
You begin the tale with Avatar Wan, so naturally
the story would circle back around and end

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:28.240
on a similar moment.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.099
The cycle of the avatar, it’s all about
the circle of life.

00:05:31.099 --> 00:05:33.151
If someone wants to cue the Lion King theme.

00:05:33.151 --> 00:05:37.200
You can let me know if you agree though, do
you think the series should end on a moment

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:40.009
that ties back with Avatar Wan?

00:05:40.009 --> 00:05:41.819
Number 4 - Azula

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:43.210
She was just so much fun.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:47.419
She was written well, got a lot of time to
develop in the narrative and was voiced by

00:05:47.419 --> 00:05:49.849
the amazing Grey Delisle.

00:05:49.849 --> 00:05:53.659
If you want to learn more about Azula after
the last airbender series, just read the comics.

00:05:53.659 --> 00:05:56.240
I’ve noticed a lot of you don’t know where
to buy them.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:01.530
If you’re local comic shop doesn’t have
them, you can find them online on comixology.com

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:04.979
I’ll be totally okay if we do not see Azula
in book 4.

00:06:04.979 --> 00:06:07.660
But it would be a lot of fun if she at least
got a name drop.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.159
Number 3 - Ozai

00:06:10.159 --> 00:06:14.270
Not quite as complex as some of the other
villains like Zuko, but largely thanks to

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:19.430
Mark Hamill’s performance and the highly
serialized nature of the last airbender series,

00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:22.540
he turned out to be a very good big bad.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:25.870
Sometimes the over-the-top crazy villains
are the best.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:30.650
Unless you count the flashbacks to his early
childhood, Ozai was always the clear villain.

00:06:30.650 --> 00:06:34.919
Very uncomplicated, he wanted to crush the
avatar and dominate the world.

00:06:34.919 --> 00:06:36.539
Very simple.

00:06:36.539 --> 00:06:42.130
It made the final arc of the last airbender
series very easy to follow.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.030
Aang needed to squish him like a bug.

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:49.300
So the entire last airbender series became
the rise of aang and the fall of ozai.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:50.449
He spiritually squashed him like a bug, but
it was still that big TKO Mike Tyson punch

00:06:50.449 --> 00:06:51.449
out ending.

00:06:51.449 --> 00:06:53.650
The bigger the villain, the more satisfying
the takedown.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:59.780
Which is why I’m not sure if Korra taking
Kuvira down will be as satisfying, we just

00:06:59.780 --> 00:07:00.780
haven’t seen enough of her.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:06.479
I’m going to withhold that judgement till
after book 4.

00:07:06.479 --> 00:07:08.490
Number 2 - Team Zaheer

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.780
One of the best villains or group of villains
in both series.

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:12.780
I also liked the character development and
execution much better too.

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.969
It felt like the Red Lotus characters got
the same attention that Amon got in Book 1.

00:07:15.969 --> 00:07:18.180
And conceptually, they were very unique in
their motivation.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:22.999
Zaheer to me felt like a very nietzschean
villain.

00:07:22.999 --> 00:07:29.810
Only in that he wanted to kill the idea of
God.

00:07:29.810 --> 00:07:31.550
Represented by the Avatar.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:36.039
He wasn’t exactly nietzschean because he
did have spiritual beliefs, nihilism is like

00:07:36.039 --> 00:07:37.219
the belief in nothing.

00:07:37.219 --> 00:07:42.279
And Zaheer very clearly believed in higher
powers than himself.

00:07:42.279 --> 00:07:46.790
Henry Rollins deserves a lot of credit for
that cool creepy performance too.

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:50.439
Something about a villain that seems so together
and calm makes him scarier.

00:07:50.439 --> 00:07:55.150
He’s not dead either, so I’ll be interested
to see how he’s referenced in book 4.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:08:00.520
But Ghazan supposedly died in the lava flow,
P’Li was killed by Suyin and Ming Hua was

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:02.259
shocked to death by Mako.

00:08:02.259 --> 00:08:06.070
So Zaheer is all by himself in prison right
now.

00:08:06.070 --> 00:08:07.720
Number 1 - Amon

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:12.060
He’s still my favorite right now just because
of the style, execution and performance of

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.150
his character.

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:17.569
I loved the costume and the grandeur of his
anti-bending campaign.

00:08:17.569 --> 00:08:22.580
He was a good analog for real life sinister
political dissidents.

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:25.620
It made his mission very relatable.

00:08:25.620 --> 00:08:29.370
Get people to believe that benders treat normal
people like second class citizens.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:33.080
So he’s going to level the playing field
until everyone is equal.

00:08:33.080 --> 00:08:35.020
Very good story arc.

00:08:35.020 --> 00:08:40.149
We only saw him for one season but I feel
like he was such a fresh challenge for the

00:08:40.149 --> 00:08:46.010
avatar and had such a tragic life story, he
ended up being one of the more interesting

00:08:46.010 --> 00:08:47.910
villains.

00:08:47.910 --> 00:08:53.160
Like Zuko if Zuko had gone darker instead
of joining team avatar.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.620
And the performance was so good.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:58.790
There are probably only a few people who could
match a performance from Steven Blum.

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.529
Such an amazing voice.

00:09:00.529 --> 00:09:03.779
Mark Hamill maybe, or Grey Delisle.

00:09:03.779 --> 00:09:08.260
Let me know who your favorite Avatar Villains
are and if you think Kuvira will go down as

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.260
one of the best.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:13.620
Don’t forget that it’s also possible that
there could be a twist before the end and

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:15.240
some other villain could manifest.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.460
The trailer doesn’t explain everything.

00:09:16.460 --> 00:09:17.800
And as a quick sidenote.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.610
If you do want to see more Steven Blum right
now, he’s one of the main characters on

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:22.610
Star Wars Rebels.

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:25.940
They’re airing the first episode on Disney
XD tomorrow night.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:30.160
I’ll be posting one more bonus video tomorrow
morning before my Episode 1 video.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:31.410
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:09:31.410 --> 00:09:32.410
Reminder too.

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:36.610
Book 4 episode 1 will post on the nick dot
com website friday sometime before 12PM pacific

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:37.610
time.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:42.260
If you watch the google play store too, sometimes
episodes post there even earlier than that.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:47.730
Right now click here for my book 4 trailer
breakdown and click here for my non spoilery

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.240
Star Wars Rebels Episode 1 review.

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:56.829
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and get ready for Korra tomorrow!

